Determine whether NEW external Web or image research is required for this presentation.

Start with false for both.

Set Web to true only when the presentation cannot be completed reliably without missing current or external facts.

Set images to true only when actual real-world visuals are needed and generated diagrams, illustrations, or existing materials would be insufficient.

Evaluate Web and images independently. Avoid optional or merely helpful research.

